 - Profiles remain at canonical dimensions and palette sizes rather than expanding to all ARC sizes; the goal was faithful semantic coverage, not unconstrained scale diversity.
 - Audit findings A1 and A2 are report-only; their generators were not modified under this assignment.
+
+## Review review-e1bae10251bf9386 — native parametric family
+
+A matched-input two-setting family was added under `workspace/parametric/` without changing the production generator or selected canonical authority.
+
+- `completion=all_colors` returns the exact canonical Racket source byte-for-byte.
+- `completion=rarest_active_color` first finds colors participating in at least one same-color diagonal pair, derives the uniquely least frequent active color from the input, and completes only that color's pairs.
+- The sampler supports 2–6 prefix-stable demonstrations and 1–4 prefix-stable queries. Its four query profiles are 10×12, 17×19, 30×30, and 25×29; the 30×30 case contains 76 nonzero cells and touches every boundary.
+- Every lesson uses three active colors with distinct occurrence counts, both diagonal orientations, repeated pairs, and an occupied companion. The first two demonstrations vary both the selected color and its count.
+- A finite bank of nine executable rivals covers all-colors, first/last/most active, rarest nonzero, all-but-rarest, count-two, and first-pair shortcuts.
+
+A 32-seed audit initially exposed a seed-22 alias where a randomized high-color singleton could make the rare color the last row-major active color. A regression test now covers all 32 seeds, and extras are placed in unused companions of separate motifs so the high-count color remains below the rare color's row-zero anchor. Final bounded evidence covers 192 episodes, 24 protected-Racket parity evaluations, and zero surviving named rivals. This is finite evidence, not a claim of universal identifiability or training benefit.
