+# Native parametric family: b37eb391ddc0
+
+`completion=all_colors` is the exact canonical program: every same-colored
+opposite-corner pair completes its 2×2 block.
+
+`completion=rarest_active_color` first finds the colors that actually participate
+in a diagonal pair, counts their occurrences in the input, and binds the unique
+least frequent active color. It then completes only that color's pairs. Step A
+therefore produces an input-dependent color that step B needs for its write mask.
+
+Inputs are matched across settings. The minimum two demonstrations change both
+the selected color and its count; every scene also contains two nonselected
+active colors, a one-cell nonactive guard, both diagonal orientations, and an
+occupied companion that the selected rule may overwrite. Four query roles cover
+transfer, larger geometry, a substantive 30×30 boundary scene, and a wide scene.
+`public_turn()` exposes all demonstrations and exactly one unlabeled query.
+
+From the packet's outer directory:
+
+```sh
+python3 review.py run python3 -m pytest -q \
+  generators/b37eb391ddc0/tests/test_parametric_rarest_active.py
+python3 review.py run python3 \
+  generators/b37eb391ddc0/workspace/parametric/audit.py \
+  --out generators/b37eb391ddc0/workspace/parametric/evidence/current/self-audit.json
+python3 review.py run python3 -m arcpuzzles parametric qualify b37eb391ddc0 \
+  --demos 3 --queries 4 --out ../checks/b37eb391ddc0/qualification --summary
+```
+
+These are reviewer-side source-bound checks only. Owner acceptance and training
+admission remain separate.
